# Do not manually redesign terrain, missions, models, textures, or world…

Do not manually redesign terrain, missions, models, textures, or world content
for the base project.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Do not manually redesign terrain, missions, models, textures, or world
  content for the base project.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency was recorded in the legacy TODO.

## Evidence

The accepted [faithful-base governance ADR](../../../adr/governance/faithful-base-and-optional-mod-boundary.md)
now makes source evidence, not operator/editor/aesthetic preference, the authority
for canonical terrain, missions, world layout, models, textures, materials,
audio, cinematics, UI, progression, tuning, and localization. It explicitly
rejects hand-edited terrain, placement, mission, material, and texture changes
without source-backed conversion evidence.

Existing world-assembly and native-asset ADRs already reject manual placement,
copy-paste, drag-and-drop production assembly, hidden editor repair, map offsets,
and replacement terrain. The remaining offset/distant-object/LOD/vehicle
questions stay open as P1 conversion audits; governance does not pre-approve any
of those corrections.
